Package: metamicrobiomeR
Type: Package
Title: Differential Abundance and Meta-Analysis of Microbiome Studies
Version: 2.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nhan", "Ho", email = "nhanhocumc@gmail.com", role = "aut"),
    person("Payton", "Yau", email = "tungon@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3283-0370")),
    person("Jun", "Chen", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "GMPR code in taxa.compare()")
    )
Description: Analyses microbiome studies one at a time and pools the results across studies.
    Studies are held in a validated study object that accepts counts or relative
    abundances, taxonomy in rank columns and study-level metadata, and can be imported from
    DADA2, QIIME 2, MetaPhlAn, BIOM, phyloseq and SummarizedExperiment objects. Per-study
    engines fit zero-inflated beta-binomial (counts), zero-inflated beta (GAMLSS),
    arcsine-square-root and centred log-ratio models, with optional subject random effects, and
    return estimates in a common effect table. Random-effects meta-analysis
    (with Hartung-Knapp inference, heterogeneity, prediction intervals, influence diagnostics,
    leave-one-out and meta-regression on study characteristics), hierarchical false discovery
    control across taxonomic ranks, alpha diversity, PERMANOVA, forest plots and provenance
    manifests complete the workflow. The zero-inflated beta model follows
    Ho et al. (2019) <doi:10.1186/s12859-019-2744-2>.
    The functions of version 1.x (taxa.compare(), meta.taxa() and others) remain available.
